		<div class="texto-blog">					
		<p>In this article we will see <strong>how to use the controllers in version 4</strong> of the codeigniter framework.</p>

		<h2 class="texto-title-blog">How do the controllers work?</h2>

		{{ include('inc/ad_defect.html.twig') }} 
		
		<p>First we have the basic structure of a controller.</p>
		


		{# 	pre mantiene el formato del texto #}
		<pre class="text-code">
		<code class="">
		class Users extends BaseController
		{
		public function index()
		{		
		
		$data['tittle'] = 'Users';		

		return view('admin/index',$data);
		}

		}
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>The controllers are located in <code>nameProject/app/Controllers</code>, every controller extends from the main controller named <strong>BaseController</strong>, which is on the same route.</p>

		{# <pre> #}
		<p>
		<code class="">

		class Users extends BaseController

		</code>
		</p>
		{# </pre> #}
		

		<h2 class="texto-title-blog">What is the BaseController?</h2>			

		<p>Here we have the BaseController which extends from Controller which is the core class of the framework, through the initController function we can automatically load services, libraries, models etc.</p>
		<pre class="text-code">
		<code class="">
		namespace App\Controllers;

		/**
		* Class BaseController
		*
		* BaseController provides a convenient place for loading components
		* and performing functions that are needed by all your controllers.
		* Extend this class in any new controllers:
		*     class Home extends BaseController
		*
		* For security be sure to declare any new methods as protected or private.
		*
		* @package CodeIgniter
		*/

		use CodeIgniter\Controller;

		class BaseController extends Controller
		{

		/**
		* An array of helpers to be loaded automatically upon
		* class instantiation. These helpers will be available
		* to all other controllers that extend BaseController.
		*
		* @var array
		*/
		protected $helpers = [];

		/**
		* Constructor.
		*/
		public function initController(\CodeIgniter\HTTP\RequestInterface $request, \CodeIgniter\HTTP\ResponseInterface $response, \Psr\Log\LoggerInterface $logger)
		{
		// Do Not Edit This Line
		parent::initController($request, $response, $logger);

		//--------------------------------------------------------------------
		// Preload any models, libraries, etc, here.
		//--------------------------------------------------------------------
		// E.g.:
		// $this->session = \Config\Services::session();
		}

		}
		</code>
		</pre>
		
		<p>Inside we have a variable <code>$data</code> which we can pass to a view.</p>
		<code class="">
		public function index()
		</code>

		
		<p>Now we have the index method, which is the first method that is executed when loading the class, unless we load the constructor.</p>
		<code class="">
		$data['tittle'] = 'Users';
		</code>

		
		<p>Finally we return a view, where the first parameter is the path of the view and which accepts as the second parameter the <code>$data</code>.</p>
		<code class="">
		return view('admin/index',$data);
		</code>

			


